<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton crop sowing rises 5.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton crop sowing rises 5.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton crop sowing rose 5.2 percent to 7.781 million acres (3.15 million hectares) in the 1996/97 (July-June) crop year from 7.393 million in 1995/96, the private Karachi Cotton Association (KCA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The area rose 3.3 percent in the main growing Punjab province and 14.4 percent in Sindh province, the KCA said.</p>
<p>Pakistan has set a cotton production target of 10 million 375-lb bales for 1996/97 crop. But ginners say the output is likely to rise to 11 million bales owing to a bumper crop, compared to 9.94 million produced in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
